#33030
book cedar~
Book: The Natural uses of Cedar~
Book: The Natural uses of Cedar~
  {030}-   {130}Cedar is a light weight and dimensionally stable wood that lies flat and 
  stays straight, which means it resists the natural tendency to crack and
  check as you might find in many other wood species.

  {030}-   {130}Western Red Cedar is incredibly thermal coefficient, meaning even on hot
  hot days it is cool to sit in.

  {030}-   {130}Its bacterial and fungal resistance coupled with the fact that cedar is
  80% the strength of Oak, makes it the most desirable wood to use for 
  outdoor building materials.

  {030}-   {130}Western Red Cedar fibers contain oils that act as natural preservatives
  to help the wood resist rot and decay making it excellent furniture
  material for moist and humid climates.

  {030}-   {130}Among other things these naturally occuring organic compounds called
  ( thujaplicins ) give off that distinct cedar aroma that is pleasent
  to humans, but a detterent to insects, moths, and other wood pests. 
  This is why cedar is a choice wood for bookshelves, dressers, and even
  pet furniture.
~
