#33031
recipe book~
Book: Real Life Recipe Book~
You see a Real Life Recipe Book here~
  {170}Ok you mudders out there you have found something that no one has done before
in Mortal Realms. And that is added an item that contained a Real Life Recipe.
This is a dish that my mother used to serve the family on a regular basis, and
has given to me and my wife for our family. Its a good meal when added with
some veggies. Give it a try sometime.

{1330}              Beef Strogainoff

  {030}Ingrediants:
  {130} - 1lb of Hamburger
 - 3 slices of Diced Bacon or 2 tablespoons of Bacon Bits
 - 1/2 Cup of Diced Onion ( I Use a 1/4 cup )
 - 1 1/2 tablespoons Flour
 - 3/4 Teaspoon of Salt and a Dash of Pepper
 - 1/4 Teaspoon of Paparika
 - 1 Can of Cream of Mushroom Soup
 - 1 Cup of Sour Cream
 - 1/2 Cup of diced olives ( Optional )

  {030}Directions:   {130}Brown ground beef in a skillet or frying pan, add onion and cook
until tender, but not brown. Drain excess fat/grease. Stir in soup and add a
half a can of water. Blend flour, salt, pepper, and paparika in the other
half a can of water. Stir in and add bacon. Cook Slowly for 20 Minutes.
Stirring frequently. ( Add Olives if olives are desired ). Stir in sour cream
and heat thoroughly.

This is best served on top of Egg Noodles ( a half of 16oz. bag usually feeds
3 - 4 servings depending on appetite ). Fresh frozen pea's makes an excellent
side dish with this meal.

  {030}Note: For those who do not eat red meat or have special diets. The Ground 
Beef can be substituted with Chicken or Pork. For those on diets. I find the
Chicken version tastes better when the Cream of Mushroom is substituted with
Cream of Broccoli. For Low Fat version the Sour Cream and soup can be
substituted with fat free or low fat Sour Creams and Soups.
~
